  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Yerevan Kiosk within its distinct four-corner canopy: faceted blue upper room with three projecting window bays, pale lower marble panels/gold grilles, long open pointed portico and pale shafts/capitals, broad lead hip/colored soffit, shallow domed chamber and a descending garden stair/balcony. Independent Sacred Relics chamber, Sofa Kiosk, Mosque, pool, freestanding fountain and general terrace remain native context. Picture-led chamber/portico eaves6.3m above a shared floor, three projecting window bays, two window levels and a low lead dome on a short octagonal drum. Heights, hidden roof/dome profile, interior arrangement, column/window counts and garden stair dimensions are reconstruction controls, not a survey. Floor is .55m above the highest native boundary sample. The lower garden flight follows the pictured2.65m descent; the coarse native grid buries much of that descent. Two ordinary Moonik2012 exterior pictures actually viewed; map name/Q6040439 corroborated by OSM v14 and Wikidata. Cross-room proportions, upper/lower opening inventory, column count, curved braces, dome/hidden roof profile and garden flight remain picture-led reconstructions. Main pavilion fit accepted as approximate; historical lower garden-level fit is explicitly not approved because the coarse grid lacks the terrace drop and buries much of the basement/stair. No custom terrain, copied inscriptions/artwork, museum furnishings or independent pool/fountain/Sacred Relics/Sofa structures. This completes one medium-fi kiosk exterior with the stated terrain limitation. Topkapi remains incomplete13/18ready; Hasoda remains an inactive terrain-fit draft."
  },
